=A. Use a supportable claim, relevant evidence, fair counterclaim, and practical rebuttal grounded in the source.#Correct. Step 1: identify the standard skill in the question. Step 2: compare the answer with the source details and the lesson model. This answer works because it protects accuracy, structure, and audience understanding.
~B. Dismiss safety concerns because they weaken the editorial.#Not correct. Choice A says 'Dismiss safety concerns because they weaken the editorial.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
~C. Claim the survey proves every student wants outdoor seating.#Not correct. Choice C says 'Claim the survey proves every student wants outdoor seating.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
~D. Invent cost details so the argument sounds complete.#Not correct. Choice D says 'Invent cost details so the argument sounds complete.', which does not fully answer this specific journalism task. Recheck the source details, the question wording, and the mapped standard before choosing the best supported answer.
}

